        "title": "Classical and Rational Choice Theories",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Classical criminology grounds crime explanation in economics: crime is a choice made by a rational actor weighing expected benefits against expected costs. Deterrence policy flows directly from this model -- manipulate the cost side of the ledger and behavior changes."
